---
import { cta, site } from '../../lib/site';

// Letter facts stay within the brief: 12 years in professional kitchens,
// now a software engineer. Photo is owner-supplied (public/founder.jpg).
---

<section id="chef" class="border-y border-hairline bg-cream">
	<!-- Inner max-width instead of on container-page: both set max-width and
	     the winner would depend on stylesheet order. Letter sits left, air right. -->
	<div class="container-page py-section-tight">
		<div class="max-w-4xl" data-reveal>
			<p class="eyebrow">From the chef</p>
			<h2 class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">Built for the kitchen work around the event.</h2>

			<div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-8 sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:gap-10">
				<!-- Paper-matted, counter-tilted to the hero ticket: a photo
				     taped up in the kitchen, cut from the same visual world. -->
				<img
					src="/founder.jpg"
					alt={`${site.founderName}, the chef who built CostCook`}
					width="384"
					height="384"
					loading="lazy"
					class="w-36 shrink-0 -rotate-[1.5deg] self-start bg-paper p-1.5 shadow-ticket sm:order-last sm:w-44"
				/>
				<div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-lede text-ink-soft">
					<p>
						I spent twelve years cooking professionally before becoming a software engineer.
						CostCook is the system I wanted when a menu had to become a quote, a shopping
						list, a prep plan, and a pack list without losing the cost along the way.
					</p>
					<p>
						CostCook is still early. A real-order demo is the clearest way to see whether
						the workflow fits your kitchen.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Deliberate exception to the no-em-dash copy rule (#49): a leading
			     attribution dash on a signature is standard letter typography,
			     not a prose em-dash. Leave it. -->
			<p class="mt-8 font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink">
				— {site.founderName}
				<span
					class="ml-1.5 inline-block size-2.5 rotate-45 bg-offwhite shadow-[inset_0_1px_1.5px_rgb(31_36_33/0.18)]"
					aria-hidden="true"></span>
			</p>

			<a href={cta.href} class="btn-quiet mt-8">{cta.label}</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
